{"affected":[{"defaultStatus":"unaffected","original_ranges":[{"lessThanOrEqual":"4.1.16","status":"affected","version":"0","versionType":"semver"}],"packageURL":"pkg:software-id/apache.org/openoffice","product":"Apache OpenOffice","vendor":"Apache Software Foundation"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-90632"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"descriptions":[{"lang":"en","supportingMedia":[{"base64":false,"type":"text/html","value":"<div>Apache OpenOffice documents can include multimedia content (audio, video, etc.)</div><div>A crafted document could exploit the GStreamer multimedia component of Apache OpenOffice version through 4.1.16 to load the contents of any local file, and include them when the document is saved or exported, for example as PDF.</div>Users are recommended to upgrade to version 4.1.17, which fixes this issue."}],"value":"Apache OpenOffice documents can include multimedia content (audio, video, etc.)\n\nA crafted document could exploit the GStreamer multimedia component of Apache OpenOffice version through 4.1.16 to load the contents of any local file, and include them when the document is saved or exported, for example as PDF.\n\nUsers are recommended to upgrade to version 4.1.17, which fixes this issue."}],"metrics":[{"other":{"content":{"text":"important"},"type":"Textual description of severity"},"scenarios":[{"lang":"en","value":"GENERAL"}]}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-552","description":"CWE-552 Files or directories accessible to external parties","lang":"en","type":"CWE"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-04T11:05:00.779Z","orgId":"f0158376-9dc2-43b6-827c-5f631a4d8d09","shortName":"apache"},"role":"cna","title":"Apache OpenOffice: Local file inclusion via GStreamer plugin"}],"assessment":{"authentication":null,"classifier_version":"1.0","confidence":"unknown","configuration":null,"entry_protocol":null,"product_class":null,"reasons":[],"relevance":"unknown"},"content_hash":"b5d6f2febd8dd04cb941d2cdc3228baf763731d55c41a22a0